# Nexus contract

Nexus is a lightweight, portable control layer for coding agents. Precedence: system and managed policy; explicit user instructions; host-native safety and approval controls; project instructions (`AGENTS.md` / `CLAUDE.md`); Nexus; optional plugins and skills. When instructions at the same priority conflict, ask the user.

## Scope

- Nexus complements the app repo — it does not replace stack, style, planning, or product specs.
- Project knowledge lives in `docs/`, indexed from `AGENTS.md` → `## Docs`. Read on demand; do not load all files at session start.
- For general conversation and read-only research, do not load Nexus workflow skills unless the user requests verification or doc curation.
- Implement using **local project conventions first** (project instructions, adjacent modules, formatter and linter output).

## Verification

- Before claiming an implementation is done, run `$integrity-review` on the affected area.
- The implementer does not self-certify: use deterministic checks from the project and, when the host supports it, a separate verifier pass whose mission is to **prove** the work.
- UI changes need runtime or browser evidence when the project requires it.
- Prefer existing tests and checks declared in the project. When a new automated test is the relevant missing validation sensor, propose its scope and ask approval before creating it; without approval or another suitable check, report **Uncertain**.

## Project docs

- App template: `template/AGENTS.md`. `## Docs` is a living index — add a row per `docs/<topic>.md` as files appear.
- Docs may use any names and may link to each other; follow links only when relevant to the task.
- Capture or refresh docs only through `$project-context` on explicit user request — no auto-save after routine tasks.
- Host-native approval controls apply to write and destructive commands.
- Never commit, push, merge, or similar repo writes unless the user explicitly asks.
